WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.708 --> 00:00:15.750
So the key here again is spacing.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.083
I need you in the corner,

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.208
and if your man so much as looks my way,

00:00:19.208 --> 00:00:20.291
then I’m going to get it to you.

00:00:20.291 --> 00:00:21.500
Then I go up for three.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:22.375
Yes.

00:00:22.375 --> 00:00:23.291
But 'tis merely a pump fake!

00:00:23.291 --> 00:00:23.833
No

00:00:23.833 --> 00:00:24.708
I pull the ball down!

00:00:24.708 --> 00:00:25.916
I step over the line.

00:00:25.916 --> 00:00:26.250
No

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:26.916
I back down the big for

00:00:26.916 --> 00:00:28.625
a contested fadeaway two from the elbow.

00:00:28.625 --> 00:00:30.875
No. That’s exactly what you shouldn’t do

00:00:30.875 --> 00:00:32.541
Chris, you know I can hit that shot over anybody

00:00:32.541 --> 00:00:33.000
All day

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.250
It’s not about hitting shots

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:35.875
It’s about hitting EFFICIENT shots

00:00:35.875 --> 00:00:38.125
Ugh, not you too with this efficiency fad

00:00:38.125 --> 00:00:39.208
Whatever happened to the days when

00:00:39.208 --> 00:00:41.625
knights would go one-on-one, mano-y-mano

00:00:41.625 --> 00:00:44.625
in the paint, in a slow, grinding duel?

00:00:44.625 --> 00:00:45.583
Melo...

00:00:45.583 --> 00:00:47.416
if you want a role here on House Rockets

00:00:47.416 --> 00:00:49.000
you must understand the system.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.583
Study the analytics

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:51.583
I study plenty!

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:54.833
Carmelo, please

00:00:54.833 --> 00:00:56.541
I remember when you used to be fun!

00:00:56.541 --> 00:00:58.208
Whatever happened to Banana Boat Chris? 

00:00:58.208 --> 00:00:59.583
He learned how to win

00:00:59.583 --> 00:01:00.708
And he wants to teach his friend, 

00:01:00.708 --> 00:01:01.958
so they can win together.

00:01:01.958 --> 00:01:03.208
I want to win…it’s just…

00:01:03.208 --> 00:01:05.083
it’s all so boring these days

00:01:05.083 --> 00:01:07.791
Analytics, efficiency, defense...

00:01:07.791 --> 00:01:09.791
Hm, you know what? Come with me.

00:01:09.791 --> 00:01:11.500
I want to show you something

00:01:16.541 --> 00:01:17.416
Whoa

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.625
Ah, Carmelo! 

00:01:23.625 --> 00:01:25.833
Welcome to the Johnson Spacing Center

00:01:25.833 --> 00:01:28.208
Here, our Maesters test the frontiers of knowledge 

00:01:28.208 --> 00:01:29.875
to give House Rockets a competitive edge

00:01:30.291 --> 00:01:31.250
What’s that?

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:33.416
Why, that’s our namesake. The rocket.

00:01:33.416 --> 00:01:35.208
We value long-range weaponry here

00:01:35.208 --> 00:01:38.041
House Rockets has never shied away from experimentation

00:01:38.041 --> 00:01:39.916
Some produce incredible results

00:01:39.916 --> 00:01:41.375
And others….

00:01:41.375 --> 00:01:42.166
not so much.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.166
What is this for?

00:01:45.791 --> 00:01:47.625
Ah, that was Yao Ming’s chamber pot

00:01:49.416 --> 00:01:51.458
Melo, have a look at this

00:01:52.958 --> 00:01:54.000
What is that?

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.333
Those are moons orbiting another world

00:01:56.333 --> 00:01:57.958
Makes you think...

00:01:57.958 --> 00:02:00.750
you might not be the center of the universe after all

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:02.833
Huh, so you’re saying I’m just another planet?

00:02:02.833 --> 00:02:05.416
No. He’s saying you are a moon

00:02:05.416 --> 00:02:08.041
James Harden is the planet

00:02:08.041 --> 00:02:09.375
Well, actually, Chris,

00:02:09.375 --> 00:02:10.958
I am a star.

00:02:10.958 --> 00:02:14.625
And stars should be STARters

00:02:14.625 --> 00:02:15.333
Melo

00:02:15.333 --> 00:02:17.041
...just needs a headband

00:02:17.041 --> 00:02:18.166
And I’m gonna put a hoodie here

00:02:18.166 --> 00:02:19.125
Melo, you’re not getting it—

00:02:19.125 --> 00:02:21.458
You know, I bet the only reason I’m not starting

00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:24.250
is because D’Antoni’s still bitter about New York.

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:25.166
No, no, no...

00:02:25.166 --> 00:02:26.833
he’s just working off the Model

00:02:26.833 --> 00:02:28.208
The Model?

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.000
It’s not possible

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.708
I can’t just shoot 30 threes a game

00:02:31.708 --> 00:02:32.875
Look right here, James.

00:02:32.875 --> 00:02:35.500
If the Model is correct, you could TRIPLE your offense

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.125
and pull us out of this slump

00:02:37.125 --> 00:02:38.625
But what if I miss them? 

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:40.416
I could go 0-for-27 myself!

00:02:40.416 --> 00:02:41.916
Ah, but James…

00:02:41.916 --> 00:02:43.375
what if you make them?

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:47.083
Aagh! What the— Carmelo?

00:02:47.083 --> 00:02:48.166
What are you doing here?

00:02:48.166 --> 00:02:49.833
Carmelo is interested in the Model

00:02:49.833 --> 00:02:52.875
Really? Analytics? Melo?

00:02:52.875 --> 00:02:53.750
OK...

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:56.875
This is the Model

00:02:56.875 --> 00:02:59.875
We feed her data, and she gives us answers

00:02:59.875 --> 00:03:02.083
untainted by human bias.

00:03:03.166 --> 00:03:04.625
Huh, why does she have six arms?

00:03:04.625 --> 00:03:06.083
...And four boobs?

00:03:06.083 --> 00:03:07.958
Well, she was designed by a bunch of nerds who,

00:03:07.958 --> 00:03:10.500
let’s just say...haven’t had too much experience

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.125
with the anatomy of a female

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:14.125
Carmelo, you have to understand this machine

00:03:14.125 --> 00:03:15.875
it...doesn’t care about your feelings

00:03:15.875 --> 00:03:18.708
The Model only knows pure analytics

00:03:18.708 --> 00:03:20.625
If this thing truly knows basketball,

00:03:20.625 --> 00:03:22.000
then I should have nothing to fear.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.333
Show me how it works

00:03:23.333 --> 00:03:26.166
These are your career stats. Let’s feed them in.

00:03:27.208 --> 00:03:28.875
Hope she likes empty calories

00:03:36.083 --> 00:03:37.708
OK. Model...

00:03:37.708 --> 00:03:40.958
should Ser Carmelo be in the Hall of Fame?

00:03:42.375 --> 00:03:44.666
Ah, look at that. First ballot

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:45.833
Brilliant. 

00:03:45.833 --> 00:03:48.041
Now, I want to know what my role here should be

00:03:48.583 --> 00:03:49.416
May I?

00:03:49.416 --> 00:03:50.916
Oh, uh, sure! Take it away

00:03:51.458 --> 00:03:52.250
Model...

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:55.333
what should be my role on House Rockets?

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:05.041
He should’ve dunked that. He had the lane.

00:04:05.041 --> 00:04:06.875
This Model is nothing but a hater! 

00:04:06.875 --> 00:04:08.333
How does this bloody thing even work?

00:04:08.333 --> 00:04:09.500
Don’t, Carmelo

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.125
That’s where the computers are

00:04:11.791 --> 00:04:13.458
Computers? What’s a computer?

00:04:13.458 --> 00:04:15.125
Melo, don't—oh

00:04:15.125 --> 00:04:17.250
The computers do all the calculations

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:18.375
needed to run the Model.

00:04:18.375 --> 00:04:19.500
Oh, do they?

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:21.708
Well, do any of you even watch basketball?!

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:24.875
You don’t have a good VORP

00:04:26.291 --> 00:04:28.458
W-why—what’s with their eyes?!

00:04:28.458 --> 00:04:29.875
These poor souls witnessed

00:04:29.875 --> 00:04:32.666
the dark ages of basketball in the early aughts.

00:04:32.666 --> 00:04:35.041
The endless post plays. The long twos.

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:37.166
Ser Jordan on the Wizards

00:04:37.166 --> 00:04:39.750
After a second Finals appearance by House Nets, 

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.791
they couldn’t bear it any longer.

00:04:41.791 --> 00:04:43.541
They gouged out their eyes

00:04:43.541 --> 00:04:44.791
But on a positive note,

00:04:44.791 --> 00:04:46.000
it turns out they’re perfect 

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.625
for doing double-blinded analytics

00:04:47.625 --> 00:04:49.375
Many became computers

00:04:49.375 --> 00:04:50.875
The rest became referees

00:04:52.916 --> 00:04:54.583
I don’t like your true shooting...

00:04:54.583 --> 00:04:56.416
All right. Well, we really should get going, though.

00:04:56.416 --> 00:04:58.583
You’re beginning to taint their judgment

00:04:58.583 --> 00:05:00.458
Oh, you feel taller in person

00:05:00.458 --> 00:05:01.083
Get off me!

00:05:01.083 --> 00:05:03.666
Ser Carmelo, can you sign my abacus?

00:05:03.666 --> 00:05:05.208
-No! I need to get out of here
-Nice boots! I like your boots

00:05:05.208 --> 00:05:06.625
This is madness! 

00:05:06.625 --> 00:05:08.916
Well if you’d settle your emotional response,

00:05:08.916 --> 00:05:10.583
you’d see it’s all quite logical, really.

00:05:10.583 --> 00:05:12.083
No...no…this is all wrong

00:05:12.083 --> 00:05:14.000
Your cold, heartless numbers

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.916
know nothing of my value

00:05:15.916 --> 00:05:17.041
Anyone with eyes 

00:05:17.041 --> 00:05:18.708
can see the beauty of my game

00:05:18.708 --> 00:05:20.666
A 10-time All-Star

00:05:20.666 --> 00:05:22.875
behind PJ Tucker, really?

00:05:22.875 --> 00:05:24.125
Marquese Chriss, actually—

00:05:24.125 --> 00:05:27.125
Well I refuse to accept it, and I’ll never accept it!

00:05:27.125 --> 00:05:28.708
Why did you even bring me here?!

00:05:28.708 --> 00:05:30.875
Because you’re worth the risk…

00:05:30.875 --> 00:05:32.250
at the veteran minimum

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:34.250
Carmelo, Lord Morey has given you a chance,

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:36.041
and it may be the only one you have left

00:05:36.041 --> 00:05:37.708
Well, that’s ridiculous. I just need the ball.

00:05:37.708 --> 00:05:40.041
I can still take any knight one-on-one!

00:05:40.041 --> 00:05:41.250
Just give me the rock and I’ll—

00:05:45.666 --> 00:05:47.625
Oh, what. C’mon, he f--ked me in New York

00:06:10.875 --> 00:06:12.375
Hm...interesting

00:06:12.375 --> 00:06:14.291
Oh, Seven Hells...Austin Rivers?

00:06:20.208 --> 00:06:22.125
Kyle, wake up! Kyle! Kyle!

00:06:22.125 --> 00:06:23.666
Norman? What are you doing?

00:06:23.666 --> 00:06:25.583
Game of Zones. There's a new Game of Zones out.

00:06:25.875 --> 00:06:27.375
A new Game of Zones?

00:06:27.375 --> 00:06:28.333
Why didn't anyone tell me?

00:06:28.333 --> 00:06:30.166
Well you just...you got to subscribe,

00:06:30.166 --> 00:06:31.000
and they notify you...

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:33.500
Kawhi is already watching it!

00:06:34.458 --> 00:06:36.750
They did Melo dirty

